d is fuse-eligible (dropping the first-attempt-exclusion clause) OR specify that the coordinator stamps budget-cap provenance onto the outcome so the fuse can exclude a first-attempt (invocation_count=1, cumulative_sleep_ms=0) defer as the prose requires.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'keyed off budget-exhaustion provenance, not the disposition value'","Plan excludes 'any retryable_deferred the shared budget did NOT itself produce at its cap (e.g. a raw first-attempt adapter transient)' and characterizes eligible defer as 'a consumed allowance (invocation_count>1 or cumulative_sleep_ms at cap)'","retry_budget.plan_next_retry returns action='defer' on the FIRST attempt when cumulative_sleep_ms(0)+delay_ms > MAX_CUMULATIVE_SLEEP_MS, i.e. invocation_count=1, cumulative_sleep_ms=0 -> Disposition.retryable_deferred","failure_policy.is_fuse_eligible discriminates purely on disposition membership {exhausted_transient, retryable_deferred}; OperationOutcome/TicketOutcome carry no field the fuse consults to recover provenance"],"finding":"The plan's fuse-eligibility rule is internally inconsistent: it mandates keying eligibility off 'budget-exhaustion provenance, not the disposition value' and excludes a retryable_deferred that the budget did NOT produce at its cap (a first-attempt adapter transient with invocation_count=1/cumulative_sleep_ms=0), yet retryable_deferred is emitted identically for a first-attempt cumulative-sleep-cap defer and a genuinely-consumed-allowance defer, and no provenance field is preserved on the outcome for the fuse to distinguish them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcb51f82ab956045d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics -> 'Eligible exhausted outcome'","norm_id":"nf23430b86a81ba55","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An adapter reports a single first-attempt transient with provider_delay_ms exceeding MAX_CUMULATIVE_SLEEP_MS on 3 tickets of one endpoint: each yields retryable_deferred at invocation_count=1 and the endpoint fuse opens, even though per the plan's stated rule no logical budget was actually exhausted"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"If a first-attempt provider-delay defer should NOT trip the fuse, have the coordinator carry the RetryPlan's invocation_count/cumulative_sleep_ms (or a boolean 'budget_capped') on the emitted outcome and gate is_fuse_eligible on it; otherwise delete the 'raw first-attempt adapter transient' exclusion clause and state that every retryable_deferred is eligible, matching a disposition-value-keyed check.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Assign ownership of the coordinator's locate(identity)->(provider, endpoint) binding resolver (endpoint-identity attribution) to T1 (or another child) so T2's fuse counters have a specified attribution source.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["T2 Attribution: 'coordinator.TicketOutcome carries identity, disposition, failure_scope but no endpoint id; the (provider, endpoint) identity ... is resolved from the coordinator's locate(identity) binding mapping'","T1 description enumerates dispositions with 'ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global scope' as failure_scope values only; neither T1's plan, ACs, nor 'Impacted sites' mention locate(identity) or a (provider, endpoint) per-outcome binding resolver","T3 shows the signature coordinator.coordinate(ticket_plans, *, execute, locate, budget_factory) — locate is an injected parameter, but no child specifies who constructs the identity->(provider, endpoint) mapping the fuse reads","container pairing: parent + 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353/d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6/dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9"],"finding":"The scoped fuse (T2) attributes each outcome to a (provider, endpoint) identity by calling coordinator.locate(identity), and explicitly states TicketOutcome carries NO endpoint id — but T1, which builds coordinator.py, never specifies producing or exposing a locate(identity)->(provider, endpoint) binding resolver or any endpoint-identity attribution. No sibling in the roster owns delivery of this binding source, on which the fuse's endpoint/provider keying (parent AC3/AC4) structurally depends.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7f7f7adfcb488292","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9 (and gap owned by none across T1/d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6)","norm_id":"nd0a28d91124bf3e5","priority":0.8,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Fuse attempts to key endpoint/provider consecutive counters but the coordinator exposes no locate binding that returns (provider, endpoint), so inferred counters cannot be attributed and the endpoint/provider thresholds (AC3) cannot be evaluated","Two exhausted outcomes on the same endpoint cannot be recognized as same-endpoint because no binding resolver ties outcome identity to an endpoint id"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance criterion/impacted-site to T1 requiring the coordinator to expose the (provider, endpoint) binding (e.g., a locate resolver or an endpoint id on TicketOutcome), and reconcile the parent's 'coordinator tags each outcome' wording with T2's 'fuse resolves via locate()' so a single owner/mechanism is named.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py: 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353 & d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Publish the full `_BUCKET_BY_DISPOSITION` projection for all seven dispositions (applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered) so AC5 exact tallies are deterministically verifiable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T2","T4"],"criteria":["E1","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7413,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 2: 'Normalize auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, and skipped dispositions'","AC5: 'applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus exit status are exact'","Only 'commit_unknown' bucket is pinned: '_BUCKET_BY_DISPOSITION[commit_unknown]==\"deferred\"'"],"finding":"The projection from the seven normalized dispositions (auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, skipped) onto the AC5 outcome buckets (applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered) is only partially specified: only commit_unknown->deferred is given via _BUCKET_BY_DISPOSITION. The bucket for exhausted_transient, permanent, auto-healed, and success is left implicit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c682db01bc2da4e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 and step 5 / AC5 / 'commit_unknown disposition' bullet","norm_id":"n47c271091f929d27","priority":0.0587,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor tabulating exact tallies must decide whether exhausted_transient counts as failed or deferred, and whether auto-healed maps to recovered vs applied — ambiguity could make the 'exact tallies' AC unverifiable."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a table mapping each of the seven dispositions to its AC bucket, e.g. success->applied, auto-healed/recovered->recovered, exhausted_transient->failed, permanent->failed, deferred(budget-capped)->deferred, commit_unknown->deferred, skipped->skipped.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile step 4's fuse-exclusion list with the detailed eligibility bullet so both consistently state that budget-capped retryable_deferred is eligible while non-budget-produced retryable_deferred is excluded.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T2","T4"],"criteria":["COH","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.701,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 4 exclusions: 'physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404, and opaque diagnostics'","Detailed bullet: action=\"defer\" -> terminal retryable_deferred ... 'the slow/rate-limited mode that never surfaces exhausted_transient'; 'Excluded: ... any retryable_deferred the shared budget did NOT itself produce at its cap'"],"finding":"Step 4's exclusion list and the detailed 'Eligible exhausted outcome' bullet describe the retryable_deferred eligibility differently: step 4 omits retryable_deferred entirely, while the detailed section says a budget-capped retryable_deferred IS an eligible terminal outcome but a non-budget-produced one is excluded. A reader consulting only step 4 would mis-count.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11394ed48adb5719","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 vs 'Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics' -> 'Eligible exhausted outcome' bullet","norm_id":"nf57225a001f520b5","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer keys the fuse counter off step 4's exclusion list alone and never counts budget-capped retryable_deferred outcomes, undercounting toward the endpoint threshold."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Amend step 4 to reference the budget-provenance rule (eligible = budget-capped exhausted_transient OR budget-capped retryable_deferred; excluded = first-attempt/non-budget transients) rather than an ad-hoc list.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessa